{"w":2400,"h":3395,"lines":[{"y":0.10747672379945983,"w":0.055631961822509762,"t":"Test 2","c":1,"x":0.2098383399733659,"h":0.013244226206317711},{"w":0.115226338704427,"h":0.01453488398216074,"t":"READING","y":0.14970930216990597,"c":1,"x":0.51646090454448013},{"y":0.2002661716862113,"t":"READING PASSAGE 1","h":0.017839352009012766,"c":1,"w":0.26789385477701821,"x":0.20968573659940282},{"x":0.20968955818156834,"y":0.23247874381432587,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading","w":0.71228810628255212,"h":0.020604694128317336,"c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.24852767950169274,"h":0.014553715960858749,"w":0.14814814249674479,"t":"Passage 1 below.","x":0.20781893269937379},{"t":"Alexander Henderson (1831-1913)","x":0.38460932474231169,"c":1,"y":0.28333813582706346,"w":0.37689715067545571,"h":0.019737214446769791},{"w":0.65058369954427087,"x":0.2487642818525658,"h":0.020979156763730633,"t":"Born in Scotland, Henderson emigrated to Canada in 1855 and became a","c":1,"y":0.31716223320917614},{"t":"well-known landscape photographer","x":0.40931227261224007,"h":0.019651478114762755,"y":0.33688528916249061,"w":0.3274647013346354,"c":1},{"t":"Alexander Henderson was born in Scotland in 1831 and was the son of a successful merchant.","y":0.3672647270681384,"w":0.69984670003255212,"h":0.016813391650663867,"x":0.20976553719342272,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.019693233099084884,"y":0.3832445049758918,"w":0.67108896891276038,"x":0.20765787431457444,"t":"His grandfather, also called Alexander, had founded the family business, and later became"},{"y":0.39808114974941322,"t":"the first chairman of the National Bank of Scotland. The family had extensive landholdings in","h":0.019244678169313412,"x":0.20564453849588177,"w":0.69982208251953115,"c":1},{"w":0.7183817545572917,"y":0.41416514988780273,"c":1,"h":0.018947600195068137,"x":0.20767288087635913,"t":"Scotland. Besides its residence in Edinburgh, it owned Press Estate, 650 acres of farmland about"},{"w":0.70599182128906257,"x":0.20770010927390406,"h":0.017177391950879084,"y":0.42999886208902138,"t":"35 miles southeast of the city. The family often stayed at Press Castle, the large mansion on the","c":1},{"w":0.72247105916341148,"t":"northern edge of the property, and Alexander spent much of his childhood in the area, playing on","h":0.018812000962112552,"c":1,"y":0.44532819248644795,"x":0.20563163793137731},{"h":0.016900001903304762,"y":0.46051372745905694,"c":1,"t":"the beach near Eyemouth or fishing in the streams nearby.","x":0.20764925830214354,"w":0.43037460327148436},{"w":0.71226181030273439,"c":1,"t":"Even after he went to school at Murcheston Academy on the outskirts of Edinburgh, Henderson","x":0.20558879270436545,"y":0.49057213880100048,"h":0.020217436081669593},{"x":0.20564560691268696,"h":0.01746395928840061,"w":0.66894719441731776,"c":1,"y":0.50691834890611542,"t":"returned to Press at weekends. In 1849 he began a three-year apprenticeship to become an"},{"x":0.20564672198602788,"t":"accountant. Although he never liked the prospect of a business career, he stayed with it to","y":0.52233870392809301,"w":0.6648245747884115,"c":1,"h":0.017548494260358871},{"t":"please his family. In October 1855, however, he emigrated to Canada with his wife Agnes Elder","w":0.71425949096679686,"c":1,"x":0.20356644978934971,"y":0.5370977544740384,"h":0.020858942128463398},{"c":1,"x":0.20550421154135706,"y":0.55272399256556959,"w":0.29680007934570313,"h":0.017182527638717304,"t":"Robertson and they settled in Montreal."},{"w":0.66293731689453117,"c":1,"h":0.020962145640235019,"t":"Henderson learned photography in Montreal around the year 1857 and quickly took it up","x":0.20350010582844674,"y":0.58179204049886135},{"w":0.6710280354817707,"h":0.016872455430676725,"y":0.59927652649960672,"c":1,"t":"as a serious amateur. He became a personal friend and colleague of the Scottish-Canadian","x":0.20563637437968255},{"h":0.017861631930365829,"x":0.2056558258765612,"c":1,"t":"photographer William Notman. The two men made a photographic excursion to Niagara Falls in","y":0.61443941670316859,"w":0.71419235229492184},{"x":0.20563574751768565,"c":1,"y":0.63005167059484257,"h":0.016882641997859715,"t":"1860 and they cooperated on experiments with magnesium flares as a source of artificial light","w":0.69570185343424473},{"t":"in 1865. They belonged to the same societies and were among the founding members of the Art","x":0.2035219818205557,"c":1,"y":0.64500249748741012,"w":0.71224355061848954,"h":0.01971140345920519},{"c":1,"w":0.71016352335611965,"h":0.018825310279118379,"x":0.20356357032231709,"y":0.66034899183852391,"t":"Association of Montreal. Henderson acted as chairman of the association's first meeting, which"},{"t":"was held in Notman's studio on 11 January 1860.","x":0.20560103123549528,"c":1,"y":0.67551881015413784,"w":0.36662541707356772,"h":0.016863097852475528},{"w":0.68335306803385409,"h":0.018228326444771903,"c":1,"t":"In spite of their friendship, their styles of photography were quite different. While Notman's","x":0.20152372333246546,"y":0.70715631623757014},{"w":0.67104802449544265,"c":1,"t":"landscapes were noted for their bold realism, Henderson for the first 20 years of his career","x":0.20354356824294656,"y":0.722313957033906,"h":0.017999687239755868},{"t":"produced romantic images, showing the strong influence of the British landscape tradition. His","h":0.016044868316470673,"c":1,"x":0.2016460927502309,"y":0.73837209287231154,"w":0.70576131184895829},{"x":0.20164609384972598,"y":0.75436046496927134,"w":0.69958847045898431,"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"t":"artistic and technical progress was rapid and in 1865 he published his first major collection of"},{"x":0.20356752640420914,"t":"landscape photographs. The publication had limited circulation (only seven copies have ever been","y":0.76852161299823496,"w":0.72451512654622396,"h":0.01749354678132653,"c":1},{"h":0.020174758875187493,"c":1,"w":0.72252202351888029,"t":"found), and was called Canadian Views and Studies. The contents of each copy vary significantly","y":0.7830307835219199,"x":0.20148528081840802},{"x":0.20354597514796591,"h":0.018374408793814467,"t":"and have proved a useful source for evaluating Henderson's early work.","w":0.52707926432291663,"c":1,"y":0.79845513926132772},{"h":0.014125327479853289,"c":1,"t":"This text is taken, for the most part, verbatim from the Dictionary of Canadian Biography Volume XIV (1911-1920). For design purposes,","x":0.20360390019978694,"y":0.82644123405337699,"w":0.70800542195638028},{"w":0.701819101969401,"y":0.83676316279941776,"t":"quotation marks have been omitted. Source: http:\/\/www.biographi.ca\/en\/bio\/henderson_alexander_1831_1913_14E.html. Reproduced","h":0.016056496628041206,"c":1,"x":0.20154797922018608},{"w":0.086419754028320334,"t":"with permission.","x":0.20164608996114849,"y":0.84883720922836614,"c":1,"h":0.0072674419910804255},{"t":"38","y":0.86337209284624106,"w":0.022633744875590028,"x":0.20164609042228732,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1}]}